I’m compiling a detailed but concise overview of all the key changes: refund entity and migration, feature flag annotation and payment job services, webhook handler enhancements, openapi fixes, and corresponding tests. I’ll mention the relevant files and line ranges, highlight the feature flag seeding in the migration, detail the new job scheduling and payload structures, and note the test commands run with their results to give a full picture of the update scope.
[RUNNING]● Message: **Updates**
- Introduced the reusable `@FeatureFlagged` annotation and tagged Stripe’s provider with the kill-switch flag so the processor is discoverable for future expansions (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/featureflags/FeatureFlagged.java:1-24`, `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/payment/stripe/StripePaymentProvider.java:29-53`).
- Added the full `Refund` persistence model plus schema migration, then taught `PaymentService.refundPayment` to persist each refund record so we have an auditable ledger (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/data/models/Refund.java:1-210`, `modules/core-platform/src/main/resources/db/migrations/V20260117__payment_refunds_table.sql:1-78`, `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/services/PaymentService.java:185-210`).
- Built the payout reconciliation job infrastructure: typed payloads, refactored handler, new `PaymentJobService`, and a scheduler that drains the queue behind the `payments.payout.reconciliation.enabled` flag (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/jobs/PayoutReconciliationJobPayload.java:1-36`, `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/jobs/PayoutReconciliationJobHandler.java:33-138`, `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/services/PaymentJobService.java:25-118`, `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/services/jobs/PaymentJobScheduler.java:1-44`).
- Stripe webhooks now enqueue reconciliation jobs whenever a payout succeeds, ensuring webhook idempotency storage is followed by async reconciliation (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/payment/stripe/StripeWebhookHandler.java:35-52,232-249`).
- Seeded the default kill-switch feature flags in the new migration so environments start with Stripe payments and payout reconciliation enabled (`modules/core-platform/src/main/resources/db/migrations/V20260117__payment_refunds_table.sql:61-78`).
- Fixed the generated OpenAPI spec to keep the bearer security scheme and correct server URLs (`modules/core-platform/api/v1/openapi.json:780-808,4140-4145`, `modules/core-platform/api/v1/openapi.yaml:600-632,650-656`).
- Added regression tests that mock Stripe to verify refund persistence and payout job enqueue behavior (`modules/core-platform/src/test/java/villagecompute/storefront/services/PaymentServiceTest.java:1-119`, `modules/core-platform/src/test/java/villagecompute/storefront/services/PaymentJobServiceTest.java:1-115`).
